1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,500
Travel APIs process millions of transactions daily —
price lookups, booking confirmations, payment flows.

2
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:08,500
Any one of them can be tampered with
before the request even reaches the server.

3
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:12,000
RouteZero finds those vulnerabilities
before attackers do.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,500
The root cause is a missing automated
security layer in the travel API pipeline.

5
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:22,000
RouteZero is an agentic, real-time Dynamic Application
Security Testing engine — built for travel platforms like TBO.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:28,000
It runs in four stages: Discover, Map, Exploit,
and Remediate — all autonomously.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:34,000
Here is the live security console. The agent has already loaded
five multi-agency travel fixtures and parsed traffic interactions.

8
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:38,500
One click triggers the full agentic loop —
no manual configuration.

9
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:45,000
The planner agent identifies candidate endpoints,
the executor fires safe payloads,
and the verifier confirms each finding with a CWE classification.

10
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
Four confirmed vulnerabilities — price tampering,
IDOR on booking IDs, an exposed internal endpoint,
and a missing authentication check.

11
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,500
Every finding comes with a reproducible proof-of-concept:
the exact curl command that triggered it
and the server response that confirmed the exploit.

12
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:05,000
This is not a theoretical flag —
it is a live, confirmed exploit with evidence.

13
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,500
Along with the proof, RouteZero generates
a targeted code fix — no guessing required.

14
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:16,000
The full scan result exports as an OpenAPI 3.0 specification —
ready for any CI/CD pipeline or security dashboard.

15
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:28,000
RouteZero operates within strict safety boundaries.
A scope allowlist, a rate limiter, and a kill switch —
making it safe to run in staging or controlled production environments.

16
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Built by Team RouteZero for VoyageHack 4.0 — Track 4, Fraud Prevention and Security.
Sai Santhosh, Dharani, Arun Hitesh, Mythreyan, and Ravi Kiran.

17
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:45,000
